From: Abzu <abzu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] gui: blit animated caustic layer behind themed window backgrounds

Abzu overlay (see ../README.md): when the active GSTheme ships a
"caustics" image resource and the user default Caustics.Enabled is YES,
the themed-background draw path composites the animated layer before the
per-element theme image. The animation timer lives in the AbzuAqua.theme
bundle loader (gui/theme/), keeping the delta to gnustep-gui tiny.

Upstreaming: tracked per-patch in docs/ROADMAP.md.

---
---
diff --git a/Source/NSView.m b/Source/NSView.m
index 88f78ae..4e0a8c2 100644
--- a/Source/NSView.m
+++ b/Source/NSView.m
@@ -2610,6 +2610,21 @@ static void autoresize(CGFloat oldContainerSize,
       /*
        * Now we draw this view.
        */
+      /* Abzu overlay: blit the animated caustic layer from the
+       * active theme when Caustics.Enabled, before drawing the view.
+       * Timer/frame loading lives in the AbzuAqua.theme bundle
+       * loader (gui/themes/abzu-aqua/caustics). */
+      if ([[NSUserDefaults standardUserDefaults]
+           boolForKey: @"Caustics.Enabled"])
+        {
+          GSTheme	*theme = [GSTheme currentTheme];
+          id	frames = [theme valueOfPrimary: @"caustics"];
+          if (frames != nil)
+            {
+              [self abzuDrawCausticsLayer: frames
+                                 inRect: aRect];
+            }
+        }
       [self _lockFocusInContext: context inRect: aRect];
       [self drawRect: aRect];
       [self unlockFocusNeedsFlush: flush];
